  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday night through Tuesday)\nIssued at 1051 PM CDT Tue Sep 15 2026\n\nBy the second half of the weekend, the anchored ridge will be \npushed to our west as the wondering upper level low moves westward\nacross FL and into the northern Gulf. Models are even more split \ntoday on what the strength and longevity of this low will be. It \nseems to stall for a little bit over the NE Gulf late Saturday\ninto Sunday before either sliding westward, or weakening and \nfading out completely. Regardless, dangerous heat will persist \ninto the later part of the weekend. Look for highs to be in the \nlower 90s in NE AL/portions of Southern Middle TN, and the mid to \nupper 90s elsewhere. Heat index values at this time look to remain\nbelow heat advisory criteria sitting around 100 degrees, however \nwe will remain in a level 2-3 HeatRisk across the TN Valley. So \nensure to be heat safe/smart. Slow down, hydrate and never leave \npeople or pets in vehicles.\n\nAn upper level trough will move across the Rockies and Northern \nPlains this weekend and into the Upper Midwest early next week, \nbut there is also uncertainty on this feature. A sfc low will move\ninto the OH Valley on Monday and try to pull a cold front towards\nthe TN Valley. Will see low to medium rain chances return \n(20-45%) on Monday, but with the front most likely stalling on \nTuesday, we won't see a frontal passage, but have rain chances \ncontinue. This will at least help the temps lower a tad with some \nseeing highs in the upper 80s Tuesday afternoon.",
